names></name><name><surname>Sandstrom</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Temple</surname><given-names>IK</given-names></name><name><surname>Youings</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Dennis</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></name><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Crolla</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The complex nature of constitutional de novo apparently balanced translocations in patients presenting with abnormal phenotypes</article-title><source>J Med Genet</source><year>2005</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15635069</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/jmg.2004.024141</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>De Gregori</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ciccone</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Magini</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Pramparo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gimelli</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Messa</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Novara</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Vetro</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Maraschio</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonaglia</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Anichini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrero</surname><given-names>GB</given-names></name><name><surname>Silengo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Fazzi</surname>